      "jobId": "55b781b6-e543-4cf1-b618-3102900a3a84",
      "prompt": "A single flat-sided hexagonal diorama tile, 32 m across, lush meadow grass cap and the hexagon side walls show a thin grass lip over dark root-filled topsoil that darkens softly downward into a near-black foot, one continuous dark earth. A single standard-gauge railway track: two steel rails with bright polished running tops fixed to evenly spaced dark timber sleepers, bedded in a low raised bank of grey crushed-stone ballast with neatly sloped shoulders runs straight between two opposite flat edges. Alongside the track sits a short raised country platform about 20 m long with a stone-flag surface, a pale stone edge and a sloping ramp at each end. On it stands a small open-fronted waiting shelter with low red-brick walls below dark oak half-timbering over cream lime-plaster panels, a steep brown clay-tile roof with gables, tall red-brick chimneys with clay pots, and small-paned timber casement windows, its roof sweeping forward into a deep timber canopy over the platform on carved timber brackets, with a slatted timber bench under the canopy, one black cast-iron lamp post, two flower tubs and a white picket fence along the back of the platform. The only things on the platform are the shelter, the bench, the lamp post and the flower tubs, stylized-real diorama miniature, real PBR materials, slightly exaggerated proportions, soft noon sun, neutral grey studio background, 35 degree three-quarter view"
